<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87931" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρό-ληψις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>preconception, mental picture</i> or <i>scheme</i> into
			which experience is fitted, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τὴν π. ἐναρμόττειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Sent.</u>
					37
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				38
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.</u>
				1p.24U.
			</span></i>(pl.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.</u>
				3p.60U.
			</span></i>(pl.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				255
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Nat.</u>
				28.4
			</span></i>(<i><span class="en">
				p.7
			</span></i> V., pl.); also in Stoic. philos., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔμφυτοι π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Chrysipp.Stoic.
					3.17
				</span></i>
			, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοινὴ π. τῶν
			ἀνθρώπων</span> Id.ib.<i><span class="en">
				2.286
			</span></i>, al., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Epict.</u>
				1.22
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in common
			use, <i>previous notion</i> or <i>conception,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				8.27.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἔχειν πάντων ἀδύνατον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					10.43.8
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Conj.</u>
				247.22
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>PFay.</u>
				124.16
			</span></i>(<span class="entity">ii A.D.</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-λημψ-</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Rhet., <i>anticipation,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπονοίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hermog.
					<u>Meth.</u>
					10
				</span></i>
			: generally, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.425
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῴων ἐνίοις σεισμῶν καὶ ὑετῶν
					ἐμπέφυκε π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Iamb.
					<u>Myst.</u>
					3.26
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν προλήψει γεγονέναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philum.
					<u>Ven.</u>
					4.5
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> simply,
				<i>taking beforehand,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅρκου, μισθοῦ,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				4.18
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				5.8
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
